6. PROCESS PLATFORMER: CONTENT
=====================================================================
For every "process" concept of the level, create one ORDER round from the
concept's data (name, summary, steps, page, sourceQuote). Some concepts also
get a CHALLENGE round.

Send Gemini (server-side only, never expose the API key) ONE request for all
process concepts of the segment, containing only those concepts' data. Use
structured JSON output mode if available.

Instructions to send to Gemini (use these rules exactly):

"You are an expert teacher turning processes into ordering challenges. Using
ONLY the concept information provided (name, summary, steps, source quote),
create one ordering challenge per concept. Rules:
1. title: a short challenge title, max 60 characters.
2. instruction: one sentence telling the student what to put in order, max 120
   characters (for example 'Put the stages of cellular respiration in the
   correct order').
3. steps: the process steps in the CORRECT order. Use the provided steps and
   keep their order. Never reorder them and never invent steps that are not
   supported by the provided information. Rewrite each step as a short, clear
   label of at most 60 characters, with no numbering such as '1.'. If more than
   8 steps are provided, merge neighboring steps so that there are at most 8.
   If fewer than 2 steps are provided, return an empty steps array.
4. For each step also provide an explanation of 1 to 2 sentences (max 200
   characters) saying what happens in this step and why it comes at this point
   in the process, for example what it depends on from the previous step.
5. decoy (optional): only when there are 4 or more steps, provide ONE plausible
   but incorrect extra step that a student could confuse with the process, for
   example a step from a similar process mentioned in the material or a common
   misconception. Give its label (max 60 characters) and whyNot (1 to 2
   sentences explaining why it does not belong in this process). The decoy must
   be clearly distinguishable from the real steps using the provided
   information. If you cannot create a good decoy, set decoy to null.
6. Include the conceptId and the page number exactly as provided.
7. Return ONLY valid JSON matching the schema. No markdown, no commentary."

PLATFORMER CONTENT SCHEMA
{
  "levelId": "ch1-L2",
  "rounds": [
    {
      "id": "ch1-L2-r1",
      "conceptId": "ch1-c4",
      "kind": "order" | "challenge",
      "title": "string",
      "instruction": "string",
      "steps": [ { "id": "ch1-L2-r1-s1", "label": "string", "explanation": "string" } ],
      "decoy": { "id": "ch1-L2-r1-d1", "label": "string", "whyNot": "string" } | null,
      "page": number,
      "sourceQuote": "string"
    }
  ]
}

VALIDATION (implement a validator; retry once with a note listing the exact
problems; if it still fails, use the offline fallback below):
- every conceptId exists in the segment and is a "process" concept
- steps has 2 to 8 items; labels non-empty, DISTINCT, within 60 characters;
  explanations non-empty and within 200 characters
- the number of steps is NOT greater than the concept's original step count
- when the step count equals the concept's original step count, each label
  must plausibly be the same step in the same position (for example share at
  least one significant word with the original step at that index); otherwise
  the round is invalid
- the decoy label must not equal (case-insensitive) any real step label
- overwrite page and sourceQuote from the course data (never trust the model)
- unique ids

OFFLINE FALLBACK (works without Gemini): build the round directly from the
concept data: labels = the concept's steps, each cut to 60 characters with an
ellipsis, up to 8 (merge any extra steps into the last label with " and
further steps"); explanation = "Step N of [concept name]." followed by the
concept summary shortened to 150 characters; decoy = null. This guarantees the
Platformer always works, even when the AI service is down.

ROUNDS PER SEGMENT
- "order" round: one per process concept. All steps shown, the student places
  them in order.
- "challenge" round: a second round for the same concept ONLY if it has 4 or
  more steps AND a valid decoy. It has the same steps plus the decoy platform,
  and the student must NOT use the decoy.
- Cap: at most 4 rounds per segment. If there would be more, drop challenge
  rounds starting from the last concept until it fits.
- Order: for each concept, the order round then its challenge round.

